# Camera Calibration

Tools for **ChArUco** and **checkerboard** camera calibration: print a board, capture photos, estimate intrinsics, export JSON / ROS YAML, undistort, and visualize distortion. PS3 Eye live capture and preview helpers are included too.

Each tool lives in its own folder with a full README (flags, examples, notes). Implementation is in `camera_calibration/`; run everything from the repo root.

## Setup

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -e .
```

Or `python -m pip install -r requirements.txt` and run from the repo root. The CLI is `python -m camera_calibration <command>` (or `camera-calibration` after an editable install).

## Tools

| Tool | Command | README |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Generate a ChArUco board | `python -m camera_calibration generate-charuco` | [generate-charuco/README.md](generate-charuco/README.md) |
| Calibrate from a folder | `python -m camera_calibration calibrate` | [calibrate/README.md](calibrate/README.md) |
| Undistort images | `python -m camera_calibration undistort` | [undistort/README.md](undistort/README.md) |
| Visualize K / distortion | `python -m camera_calibration visualize` | [visualize/README.md](visualize/README.md) |
| Diagnose a capture set | `python -m camera_calibration diagnose` | [diagnose/README.md](diagnose/README.md) |
| Live ChArUco (PS3 Eye) | `python live-calibration/live_charuco_calibration.py` | [live-calibration/README.md](live-calibration/README.md) |
| PS3 Eye preview / focus | `python ps3eye-tools/test_ps3eye_preview.py` | [ps3eye-tools/README.md](ps3eye-tools/README.md) |

## Examples

Print a tiled A1 board, then calibrate from photos of it:

```bash
python -m camera_calibration generate-charuco \
  --paper A1 --tile-paper A3 --margin 10 \
  --squares-x 7 --squares-y 10

python -m camera_calibration calibrate path/to/images \
  --board charuco \
  --squares-x 7 --squares-y 10 --square-size 79.14 \
  --dictionary DICT_4X4_50 --auto-select \
  --camera-name ps3eye
```

Same square-count flags work for a checkerboard (`--board checkerboard`). Then undistort or inspect the result:

```bash
python -m camera_calibration undistort path/to/photo.jpg \
  --calibration output/ps3eye-charuco-simple.json \
  --output output/undistorted/photo.jpg

python -m camera_calibration visualize output/ps3eye-charuco-simple.json
```

Count **squares** (not inner corners) for both board types. `--square-size` is the measured edge of one square.

## Layout

```
camera_calibration/   # library + unified CLI
generate-charuco/     # board PDF/PNG
calibrate/            # folder calibration + ROS YAML notes
undistort/
visualize/
diagnose/
live-calibration/     # PS3 Eye live ChArUco
ps3eye-tools/         # PS3 Eye preview / focus
docs/images/
```
